  "resolved_items": [
    {
      "item": "judge classifications differ",
      "resolution": "The selected mathematical assignment claim is faithful-equivalent under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation Q8. The disagreement is resolved by inspecting the supplied integral specifications and checking applicability constructively, rather than by preferring one judge.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 8, Section 1.4, specifies cellwise material averaging without a formula. Q8 separately selects normalized integration. D003–D004 specify that construction, and the native supplement identifies the integral and its relevant laws."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge requested adjudication",
      "resolution": "Both requested subjects have been rechecked: the supplement resolves the integration operator, and the cellwise construction does not lose the selected physical assignment capability through its partition representation.",
      "primary_evidence": "The supplement supplies integral_def, L1.integralCLM', SimpleFunc.integral_eq_sum, integral_const, integral_congr_ae, and restriction laws. D005 also permits a singleton-index partition with domain and sole region equal to any given measurable physical cell."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge classification is undetermined",
      "resolution": "The identified uncertainties no longer prevent an interpretation-qualified equivalence judgment. The printed source's original freedom to choose an appropriate material average remains unresolved by the book and is preserved separately.",
      "primary_evidence": "The source images distinguish the explicit solution-q average on printed page 5 from unspecified material averaging on printed page 8. The recorded comparison rule expressly supplies Q8 as a separate convention for this row."
    },
    {
      "item": "blind translator left dependency_coverage item D047 unclear",
      "resolution": "D047 is the Bochner integral in the supplied environment. Its admitted-input branch integrates the L1 equivalence class through the continuous extension of simple-function integration. Completeness and cellwise integrability select this branch in the target. This conclusion follows from declaration specifications, not the operator name or provenance hashes alone.",
      "primary_evidence": "The native supplement's integral_def distinguishes completeness and integrability branches; integral_eq identifies the admitted branch with L1.integral. L1.integral_def, L1.integralCLM', and SimpleFunc.integral_eq_sum identify the continuous extension and measure-weighted simple-function sums."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C02 unclear",
      "resolution": "Cell indices, spatial points, material-field values, and assigned cell values retain their respective roles. Real Banach spaces provide an ambient domain for the selected vector-valued integral and include ordinary scalar and finite-dimensional material-parameter collections. The theorem does not claim that every possible material model must have this type. Its arbitrary measure parameter can be instantiated with physical volume without identifying arbitrary measures as physically appropriate.",
      "primary_evidence": "The elaborated target separates materialParameter : Point → Parameter from assigned : Cell → Parameter and explicitly quantifies physicalVolume : Measure Point. D007, D017, and D019 supply completeness and the real normed vector-space structure. Printed page 8 fixes no dimension or parameter type."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C04 unclear",
      "resolution": "Positive finite volume and integrability are Q8's conditions, not newly discovered printed hypotheses. Measurability makes restriction to a physical cell precise. Exact disjointness does constrain the supplied grid object, but does not prevent recovering the selected per-cell assignment for measurable cells sharing boundaries: apply the theorem separately to singleton partitions of the original regions and assemble the explicit average function.",
      "primary_evidence": "D005 accepts a singleton cell type, domain R, and sole region R whenever R is measurable; disjointness then has no distinct-index case. D003–D004 determine the value on R independently of all other cells. This construction requires neither deleting boundary points nor changing their measure."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C05 unclear",
      "resolution": "The first conjunct realizes the selected assignment capability. Uniqueness, locality, and constant reproduction follow from the selected integral expression and do not add independent physical assumptions. The source's qualitative suitability assessment motivates this capability; it is not a quantitative performance conclusion omitted from the target.",
      "primary_evidence": "Printed page 8 links suitability to cellwise assignment. D003 includes equality to D004. The supplement supplies integral_congr_ae, integral_const, and restrict_apply_univ, which establish the remaining identities under the target's conditions."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C06 unclear",
      "resolution": "The relevant operators are resolved: D004 uses real scalar multiplication by reciprocal cell measure and the integral under measure restriction; D013 is restricted-measure integrability; D028 is pointwise equality on the cell. The supplied scalar-action projections preserve the given real module action, and the set-order projections make D061 ordinary empty-intersection disjointness. No disputed operator remains opaque in a way material to this target.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003–D004, D013, D028, D039, D044–D055, and D056–D070 expose the formula and instance chains. The native supplement expands restriction, integrability, and the previously opaque D047 integral."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C07 unclear",
      "resolution": "Uniqueness concerns assignments equal to one fixed normalized-integral expression, not uniqueness among all appropriate averaging rules. Locality and constant reproduction are consequences of that expression. Consequently, the extra conjuncts do not establish a strict increase in mathematical strength over Q8's prescribed construction, and reduced applicability is not being counted as strength.",
      "primary_evidence": "The uniqueness antecedent requires IsCellVolumeAverage for the fixed field, measure, and regions; D003 includes equality to D004. The supplement's integral_congr_ae and integral_const establish the other equalities."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C10 unclear",
      "resolution": "The arbitrary-measure and Banach-space formulation abstracts the same normalized integration construction. Physical instances are obtained by specialization; conversely, all target conjuncts follow from that construction in the abstract setting. Exact partition requirements do not obstruct recovering the source's cellwise capability, because each original measurable cell can be treated as a singleton partition. No claim of equivalence across every averaging rule or every unspecified material type is made.",
      "primary_evidence": "The target has no finiteness, countability, Euclidean-dimension, continuity, or conservation-form requirement. D005 permits singleton partitions, while D004 depends only on the individual region, field, and measure. Q8 selects normalized integration while preserving other model-dependent rules."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item C11 unclear",
      "resolution": "The target excludes null and infinite-volume cells and nonintegrable original restrictions, as Q8 requires. Completeness prevents the incomplete-space zero branch. A comparison field equal on the measurable cell agrees almost everywhere under the restricted measure and inherits its integrability there; arbitrary values outside the cell cause no problem. Shared boundaries need not be assumed null for the singleton-partition recovery argument.",
      "primary_evidence": "hpositive, hfinite, hintegrable, and CompleteSpace appear in the explicit target. D028 specifies equality on the region. The supplement gives restrict_apply', integral_def, and integral_congr_ae. D005 permits retaining an entire original region in a singleton partition."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left semantic_checklist item N06 unclear",
      "resolution": "Existence and uniqueness are well-defined for the selected assignment. They concern neither physical model uniqueness nor PDE well-posedness. Nonvacuity holds with physical, nonconstant data: on the two Lebesgue-measured cells (0,1] and (1,2], a material parameter equal to 1 on the first and 2 on the second is integrable and has distinct averages 1 and 2.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003 fixes each assigned value to D004. D005 supports this nonempty measurable partition. The supplement gives Real.volume_Ioc, integral_const, and integral_congr_ae, establishing positive unit volumes and the stated averages."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication translation_implies_source unclear",
      "resolution": "Under Q8, this direction is yes. The resolved translation supplies normalized material integration over each physical cell, permitting equal or unequal assigned values. Physical grids represented as disjoint measurable regions instantiate the target directly; if original cells share boundaries, singleton partitions recover their unchanged individual averages.",
      "primary_evidence": "The first target conjunct and D003–D004 give the required cellwise assignment. D005 supports the singleton construction. Printed page 8 requires assignment through averaging over each corresponding cell volume, without prescribing boundary ownership."
    },
    {
      "item": "round-trip judge left implication source_implies_translation unclear",
      "resolution": "Under Q8, this direction is yes. Define the assignment by the selected normalized integral. Equality to this expression gives certification and uniqueness. Restricted integral congruence gives locality. The integral of a constant is cell measure times that constant, and positive finite measure permits cancellation. These deductions hold throughout the target's stated domain.",
      "primary_evidence": "D003–D004 supply certification and the selected expression. The supplement supplies integral_congr_ae, integral_const, restrict_apply_univ, and the admitted-input characterization of the Bochner integral. The target explicitly supplies all required analytic conditions."
    }
  ],
  "implications": {
    "lean_implies_source": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation Q8, instantiate the measure with physical volume and the parameter space with the real scalar or vector ambient space of the material data. The first conjunct assigns each cell its normalized material integral, using the same region in the numerator and denominator. Different cell values are permitted, not required. Exact partition representation does not remove the selected cellwise capability: any measurable physical cell can be used unchanged as a singleton partition, after which the explicit averages assemble into a cell-indexed assignment. The theorem does not exclude other averaging rules or assert quantified numerical suitability."
    },
    "source_implies_lean": {
      "verdict": "yes",
      "reasoning": "Under Q8, interpreted through ordinary normalized integration and its relevant admissibility conditions, take assigned(c) = ((μ(R(c))).toReal)⁻¹ • ∫ f d(μ.restrict R(c)). D003 then certifies every value. Any other certified assignment equals this expression at every cell, so function extensionality gives uniqueness. Pointwise equality on a measurable region implies restricted almost-everywhere equality, giving locality by integral_congr_ae. integral_const and restrict_apply_univ give the constant integral as real cell measure times the constant; positive finite volume permits reciprocal cancellation. The supplied native specifications justify these deductions for the target's complete real normed parameter spaces and arbitrary measures. These are consequences of Q8's construction, not laws explicitly printed in Section 1.4."
    }
  },
  "classification": "faithful-equivalent",
  "accepted": true,
  "remaining_uncertainties": [
    "The printed source alone does not determine the appropriate material-averaging formula or its analytic domain. Acceptance is exclusively under the recorded coordinator-selected interpretation Q8; it does not resolve that original source ambiguity or extend to other material-averaging prescriptions."
  ],
  "findings": [
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "interpretation-qualified-acceptance",
      "evidence": "Printed page 8 leaves material averaging unspecified, whereas Q8 selects normalized integration. Printed page 5 explicitly defines normalized averaging for the distinct solution quantity q.",
      "impact": "The accepted result must be reported as faithful under Q8, without attributing its formula, admissibility conditions, or operator identities to explicit printed assertions."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "boundary-applicability",
      "evidence": "D005 requires exact disjointness for a supplied partition, but permits each measurable original cell as the sole region of a singleton partition. D004 depends only on that cell's region, measure, and field.",
      "impact": "Direct representation of an overlapping family differs from recovery of its cellwise averages. The latter preserves the selected assignment claim without assuming boundary measure zero or silently deleting boundary contributions."
    },
    {
      "severity": "note",
      "category": "relative-uniqueness",
      "evidence": "D003 requires equality to the fixed normalized-integral expression, and the uniqueness conjunct quantifies only over assignments satisfying D003.",
      "impact": "The theorem establishes uniqueness for the selected prescription, not uniqueness of physically appropriate material models."
    }
  ],
  "rationale": "Independent inspection of the attached source images and exact inline declarations resolves the disputed semantics. The native supplement identifies the integral by its construction and characterizing laws, rather than by its name or hashes. A singleton-partition argument resolves the boundary-applicability concern without additional geometric assumptions. All four target conjuncts follow from the selected normalized-integral construction, and a nonconstant physical example establishes nonvacuity. Both implications therefore hold under Q8, supporting faithful-equivalent rather than faithful-stronger. No tools, target proof, or independent hash recomputation were used."
}
